{"id": "EUVD-2026-80555", "enisaUuid": "70be8ea6-61ed-33ba-8af6-836c8c13191f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/vfio-ap: Fix NULL deref in status_show() during queue probe\n\nWhen vfio_ap_mdev_probe_queue() creates the sysfs attribute group,\nthe queue's driver data has not yet been set. A concurrent read of\nthe 'status' attribute can therefore call dev_get_drvdata() and\nget NULL, which is then passed directly to\nvfio_ap_mdev_for_queue() where q->apqn is unconditionally\ndereferenced, causing a NULL pointer dereference.\n\nFix this by acquiring the update locks before calling\nsysfs_create_group(). The status_show() function acquires\nguests_lock before reading the driver data, so any concurrent\nread will block until after dev_set_drvdata() has been called\nand the update locks are released.\n\nAs a bonus, the APQN no longer needs to be read from the queue\nstruct after allocation \u2014 it can be read directly from apdev\nbefore allocation and stored in a local variable, which is then\nassigned to q->apqn once the allocation succeeds.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31fa0a8a3c337ed2d200166d6926ab23c14f8b2e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e102ce0f4af99dff769a4b1b4daa4cc6bd5ad2d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69632952aca04caa71e49953b6949fc04e788e67", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7db2511fc601ca3a6e3fb1bdce02261c3c3167c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd6f4ef6f8a37412909ad787c837332fb070159c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89955", "GHSA-6vjc-f3pw-3x6w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00c0ed26-94c3-39d7-b21b-b6a51af1f531", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "063c292d-30a2-378d-bf6b-0d2424246d2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "0c8ace55-d12f-359d-8149-783563aa326d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "260f3ea141382386e97611e7c2029bc013088ab1 <31fa0a8a3c337ed2d200166d6926ab23c14f8b2e"}, {"id": "2e2f53b0-211a-3a67-a1ce-84dc5b7a61fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "3c5dea9e-b409-37f5-a10d-b5bcf6f92710", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "44408102-ced6-33b6-9019-e2888bf311fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "69474e71-dac2-331a-8545-8dd6c97a3777", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "260f3ea141382386e97611e7c2029bc013088ab1 <dd6f4ef6f8a37412909ad787c837332fb070159c"}, {"id": "7bc89922-3ef2-3383-98ab-ce0c1b8f7e17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "260f3ea141382386e97611e7c2029bc013088ab1 <7db2511fc601ca3a6e3fb1bdce02261c3c3167c3"}, {"id": "b508bbc3-aab2-36b1-ae83-cdb64dcac614", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cb2f34a6-b0c1-36b4-8d23-364eaee1400d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "d75f337e-9cb2-3e5b-9db2-806c35cba0a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "260f3ea141382386e97611e7c2029bc013088ab1 <69632952aca04caa71e49953b6949fc04e788e67"}, {"id": "efd371b9-8038-34e1-a65c-4e3aae5dac9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "260f3ea141382386e97611e7c2029bc013088ab1 <e102ce0f4af99dff769a4b1b4daa4cc6bd5ad2d9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8d420f52-9484-30f9-9c29-9f31bd53a6b8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}